line 47, 48, 49, 51, 52, 53, 59, 60, 61, 63, 64, 65, 67, 68, 69, 71, 72, 73, 75, 76, 77, 79, 80, 81, 83, 84, 85, 87, 88, 89 missed: bug SUB-1154 tsc rejects a condition that is always truthy or always falsy
line 105, 106, 107, 108, 110, 111, 112, 113 type: by-design spec §Excluded-Features there is no `any`, so `let b = null` is `null`, where tsc makes it an evolving `any`
line 101, 102, 103 type: artifact tsc's baseline types the original non-strict `var a = true`, which it doesn't narrow; strict tsc narrows `a` to `true` here (and to `never` after the endless `while`)
